    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697779/group-manager-education-strategic-projects": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional Administration 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Arts 1 Level / Salary HEW10A ($191,131) 1 New Search Group Manager, Education & Strategic Projects Job No.: 697779 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 3-year fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $191,131 pa Level 10A (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them About Us Monash Arts is one of Australia’s largest and most vibrant arts faculties, renowned for its breadth across the humanities, performing arts, languages and social sciences. With a strong commitment to interdisciplinary innovation, the Faculty delivers world-class programs through six schools and across six campuses—both locally and internationally—spanning undergraduate to postgraduate study and research. Our academic community is distinguished by its research excellence and deep engagement, bringing cutting-edge scholarship into the classroom to inspire the next generation of global thinkers and leaders. The Opportunity Reporting to the Faculty General Manager, the Group Manager provides high-level leadership for the Faculty's education governance, regulatory compliance, strategic planning and operational delivery. Serving as the principal deputy to the Faculty General Manager, this role acts as the primary adviser on academic policy implementation, quality assurance and large-scale transformation initiatives while leading key Faculty projects. Key Responsibilities include: Lead end-to-end delivery of strategic education projects, from scoping through to evaluation Partner with the Deputy Dean Education on curriculum transformation, student experience initiatives, and enrolment strategies. Manage stakeholder engagement across academic, professional and executive communities Provide authoritative advice on education policy, governance and continuous improvement Lead a team, building capability and maintaining momentum across concurrent workstreams About You You are an accomplished operational leader with a strong background in higher education governance, strategic program delivery and large-scale transformation. You bring: Demonstrated experience managing complex projects in a higher education or similarly regulated environment Strong understanding of curriculum governance frameworks and academic quality processes Proven ability to influence and communicate effectively with senior stakeholders Experience leading or developing professional staff in a collaborative team setting Postgraduate qualifications in a relevant discipline, or equivalent professional experience About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply To apply, submit your CV and a 1-2 page cover letter outlining your suitability for the role considering the Key Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Dr Sarah Stow, Faculty General Manager, sarah.stow@monash.edu , +61 (0)422 269 167 Position Description: Group Manager, Education & Strategic Projects Applications Close: Tuesday 15 September 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Group Manager, Education & Strategic Projects