      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Scholarship 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Arts 1 Level / Salary New Search PhD Scholarships: Shaping AI’s Future Job No: 697891 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 3.5-year fixed-term appointment Remuneration: The successful applicant will receive a Research Living Allowance, at current value of $41,100 AUD per annum 2027 full-time rate (tax-free stipend), indexed plus allowances as per RTP stipend scholarship conditions at: www.monash.edu/graduate-research/future-students/scholarships/scholarship-policy-and-procedures . The Opportunity Artificial Intelligence – particularly generative AI – is transforming society faster than we can understand it. This gives rise to many questions around AIs influence on social cohesion, the nature of knowledge production and education, cultural advancement, geopolitical challenges, national security, trust in institutions, digital humanities, intimate and personal relationships with AI, environmental impact, and broader questions related to ethics and governance. This creates an urgent need to investigate these many and varied issues to inform future decision-making and to ensure the Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences plays a vital role in driving transformative change toward a sustainable and equitable future with AI. Monash Arts is seeking innovative and socially-conscious researchers who are driven to create meaningful change. Understanding how AI can boost sovereign capability, strengthen national security and build our economic resilience is important. But Monash Arts goes further. We ask questions about how human dimensions - our values, cultures, ethics, politics, languages, histories, health, (mis)communications, geographies, creative practices, policies and institutions - are shaping and being shaped by AI. Research in the Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (HASS), is more critical than ever before. HASS disciplines offer the tools to unpack the social and ethical complexities of AI and how these shape policies that are not only effective, but are also just and inclusive. Up to five PhD scholarships are available. These scholarships will be awarded to competitive applicants who are interested in advancing research to tackle the contemporary and future challenges associated with AI and the resultant digital and societal transformations. We seek to recruit curious individuals to work alongside a number of exciting research projects underway at Monash Arts. From exploring youth well-being and mental health, to the future of music, and inclusive communications for CALD communities – we have an exciting research program for those ready to take the next step in their career and academic journey. Below are a series of suggested project titles proposed by internationally-recognised scholars who are looking to expand their research teams. Understanding AI companionship to enhance the safety and wellbeing of young people ( Dr Claire Tanner ) Public resistance to (and rejection of) AI in everyday life ( Prof. Neil Selwyn ) AI for Inclusive CALD Ageing and Care Communication ( Dr Hui Huang ) AI and the Future of Democratic Life: Participation, Persuasion and Public Trust ( Dr Charles Crabtree ) From generative AI to generative futures in music: mapping future professionalism for evolving music labour markets ( Dr Rod Davies and Dr Nicole Canham ) Human Craft, AI and the Future of Screen Aesthetics ( Dr Elliott Logan ) Human Labour and Automation in the Warehouse and Logistics Industry ( Dr Christopher O'Neill ) Auditing Algorithms: Detecting and reducing discrimination in AI-Driven Decisions ( Dr Charles Crabtree ) The changing nature of digital inequalities in an age of AI ( Prof. Neil Selwyn ) If successful, you will join Australia’s largest University which has six globally networked campuses and international alliances across Asia and Europe. Successful candidates will be based at either the Clayton or Caulfield campus in Melbourne, Victoria, and will have access to international mobility grants, professional development training and opportunities for industry engagement. Monash Arts is a diverse and vibrant faculty which advances disciplinary, multi- and inter-disciplinary research that operates at a multitude of scales: from the individual, to communities, societies, regions, nations and international. Candidate Requirements We welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds in the humanities, social sciences and creative arts who are committed to addressing contemporary social, cultural, political and environmental challenges associated with the rapid rise of AI systems in Australia and beyond. The selection committee will prioritise applicants who hold an Australian (or equivalent international) Honour’s or Master’s degree (in a cognate field aligned with proposed research topic) with evidence of a significant research component, and with first-class Honours/H1 (equivalence) awarded. Details of eligibility requirements, including English-language proficiency skills, to undertake a PhD in the Faculty of Arts are available at arts.monash.edu/graduate-research/application-process/ . Applicants should ensure they familiarise themselves with these requirements before deciding whether they should apply Scholarship holders must be enrolled full-time and on-campus. Please note: applicants who already hold a PhD will not be considered. The successful applicant is expected to commence no later than 12 th March 2027 . Enquiries You are required to discuss your research proposal with an aligned prospective supervisor (see links alongside suggested project titles) before you submit an application. How to Apply Applications shall comprise: A cover letter that includes a brief statement of the applicant’s suitability A draft Research Proposal that (i) fits within the scope of this call for research, (ii) aligns, where feasible, with one of the proposed topics, and (iii) demonstrates some understanding of the area of research (e.g., discipline or field of study). A detailed curriculum vitae, including a list of any published works, conference presentations and relevant work experience A full statement of academic records, degree certificates and official grading system (if available), supported by scanned copies of relevant certified documentation English language proficiency test results (if applicable) Names and contact details of 2 academic referees Once you have discussed your proposal with the prospective project supervisor, please submit your application via My.App and upload all supporting documentation in pdf format : Select Admission Only as the Application Type Select ‘Yes’ to indicate that you are applying for a scholarship for this research and enter “PhD Scholarships: Shaping AI’s Future” as the scholarship name under Research Program Funding of the application. Select the relevant project supervisor as the name of the proposed main supervisor (final supervision arrangements to be confirmed upon appointment). Applications Close: Wednesday 30 September 2026, 11:55 pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes PhD Scholarships: Shaping AI’s Future Clayton campus 30 Sep 2026 Monash Arts is seeking innovative and socially-conscious researchers who are driven to create meaningful change. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes PhD Scholarships: Shaping AI’s Future Clayton campus 30 Sep 2026 Monash Arts is seeking innovative and socially-conscious researchers who are driven to create meaningful change. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
