    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/693436/clinical-trials-program-manager": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional Research (Admin. Support) 1 Locations Off-campus St Kilda Road 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary HEW 8 ($124,343 - $137,251) 1 New Search Clinical Trials Program Manager Job No.: 693436 Location: 509 St Kilda Road, Melbourne Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12-month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $124,343 - $137,251 pa HEW Level 08 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Looking for a high-impact role to anchor your expertise in a world-class research environment? Monash University’s Transfusion Research Unit (TRU) is an internationally recognised research powerhouse. We are the forces behind the NHMRC Blood Synergy program—addressing critical evidence gaps in blood cancers, major haemorrhages, and critical care. We are seeking an execution-focused Program Manager for a fixed-term leave replacement to step in and seamlessly drive our operations forward. With 8 active clinical trials in progress, we need someone who can hit the ground running to oversee operations steamline processes and keep a dedicated team on track. If you are a high-level program manager who thrives under broad direction and enjoys full ownership of complex portfolios, this is your next move. Support the conduct of clinical trials, including staff training, project monitoring, data collection, preparation of results/reports, and investigator communication. Assist with managing operations across the research unit, including monitoring assigned tasks to ensure clinical trials milestones are reached. Manage the implementation of improvements across the trials group, including streamlining processes, practices, and developing templates for unit-wide use. Source and assign trials resources, support procurement tender processes, and negotiate/manage contracts with external providers. Undertake research and analysis on current clinical practices to devise solutions and provide practical, expert advice to senior leaders on trials-related issues. Exercise strong budget management for the unit's clinical trials in partnership with the Operations Manager. Develop and maintain strong partnerships with investigators and key project stakeholders by networking, liaising, presenting information, and coordinating/attending meetings. About you: You are an operational strategist. You understand the compliance realities of clinical trials but approach them with a pragmatic, solution-oriented mindset. Because this is a leave replacement role, your ability to quickly assimilate new concepts and establish immediate credibility is crucial. The Requirements: Postgraduate qualifications (or progress toward them) with extensive experience, or an equivalent high-level combination of training and management expertise. A proven track record of successfully steering medium-to-large-scale clinical trials through to completion on time and on budget. Exceptional planning skills with experience establishing priorities, shifting resources, and meeting tight deadlines. Highly developed relationship management and negotiation skills to effectively interface with diverse stakeholders. Advanced computer literacy and experience working with clinical trial systems and software platforms. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Ms Naomi Aoki, Business Projects Manager, Naomi.Aoki@monash.edu Position Description: Clinical Trials Program Manager Applications Close: Sunday 13 September 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Clinical Trials Program Manager St Kilda Road HEW 8 ($124,343 - $137,251) 13 Sep 2026 The School of Public Health and Preventive Medicine is seeking a Clinical Research Associate to support the Transfusion Research Unit in delivering high-impact clinical research programs. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Clinical Trials Program Manager St Kilda Road HEW 8 ($124,343 - $137,251) 13 Sep 2026 The School of Public Health and Preventive Medicine is seeking a Clinical Research Associate to support the Transfusion Research Unit in delivering high-impact clinical research programs. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
