, and continuous improvement across global cyber security operations! PhD Scholarship Opportunity: Developing the Next Generation of Evidence-Based Rheumatology Researchers St Kilda Road 4 Oct 2026 Applications are invited for a fully supported PhD scholarship at Monash University to undertake innovative research in the development, implementation and evaluation of living clinical practice guidelines in rheumatology. Based within the Australia and New Zealand Musculoskeletal (ANZMUSC) Clinical Trials Network, this project offers the opportunity to contribute to internationally recognised research that directly informs clinical care for people with rheumatic diseases.. Clinical Research Associate St Kilda Road HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 20 Sep 2026 Seeking a Clinical Research Associate to support the Transfusion Research Unit in delivering high-quality, investigator-initiated clinical trials. In this role, you’ll oversee trial activities from site set-up and staff training through to data monitoring, reporting and completion, contributing to high-impact research outcomes. Professor and Director of the Monash Institute of Pharmaceutical Sciences Parkville campus - A competitive remuneration package will apply 5 Oct 2026 Monash University is searching for an exceptional leader to become the next Director of the Monash Institute of Pharmaceutical Sciences (MIPS), one of the world's leading pharmaceutical research institutes. School Manager, School of Media, Film and Journalism, Faculty of Ar Caulfield campus HEW 8 ($124,343 - $137,251) 17 Sep 2026 As the School Manager, you will play a pivotal role in driving the operational leadership and strategic success of the School of Media, Film and Journalism within the Faculty of Arts. Principal Enablement Lead Clayton campus HEW10A ($191,131) 17 Sep 2026 Drive the future of AI-driven research as the Principal Enablement Lead for Project MAVERIC, the University’s AI supercomputing platform. Executive Assistant Clayton campus HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 17 Sep 2026 The Office of the Provost and Senior Vice-President has an exciting opportunity for an Executive Assistant. Deputy Director, Development - Global Markets Clayton campus HEW10A ($191,131) 17 Sep 2026 This is an exciting opportunity to play a key role in contributing directly to the pursuit of Monash University’s ambitious fundraising growth targets and position Monash as an exceptional and truly international university with scale and reach. Deputy Director, Development - Foundation Relations Clayton campus HEW10A ($191,131) 17 Sep 2026 This role offers a unique opportunity to help shape major philanthropic partnerships that directly support Monash’s research and education priorities. Clinical Site Administrator Other HEW 5 ($86,344 - $99,179) 16 Sep 2026 Support rural medical education through student placements, administration and pastoral care across Gippsland, working with diverse stakeholders. Group Manager, Education & Strategic Projects Clayton campus HEW10A ($191,131) 15 Sep 2026 Serving as the principal deputy to the Faculty General Manager, this role acts as the primary adviser on academic policy implementation, quality assurance and large-scale transformation initiatives while leading key Faculty projects. Research Fellow in Medicinal Chemistry Parkville campus Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 22 Sep 2026 Join the Faculty of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences as a Research Fellow in the Medicinal Chemistry Theme working with the development of small molecule enzyme inhibitors. Monash/Bayreuth Double PhD Degree Opportunity - Accelerating organic semiconductor discovery with generative AI, molecular dynamics and DFT Clayton campus 30 Nov 2026 As part of this program (integrated within the DFG-funded IRTG 2818 / OPTEXC framework), candidates complete an extended research stay of 6 to 12 months at the partner institution. Doctoral researchers gain access to cross-continental industry links, specialized facilities, and dual academic networks, graduating with two doctoral degrees to maximize global career impact. Associate Professor - Regenerative Medicine Clayton campus, Other Level D ($181,629 - $200,092) 11 Oct 2026 As an Associate Professor in Regenerative Medicine, you will provide academic leadership across teaching, research and postgraduate education at ARMI. PhD Scholarship - Revitalising Informal Settlements and their Environments (RISE) Caulfield campus 28 Sep 2026 RISE is an internationally recognised interdisciplinary research program developing and evaluating nature-based and hybrid infrastructure to improve health, environmental quality and climate resilience in informal settlements. As the program moves from successful pilot projects towards municipal and national implementation, these PhD projects investigate the scientific, technical and institutional innovations required to enable large-scale impact. More Jobs 43 Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Fellow Clayton campus Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 7 Oct 2026 Working within an active research group, this position will be in support of a project to develop and demonstrate micro-scale intracranial probes to sense the extremely small magnetic fields resulting from the currents flowing along nerve cells due to brain activity. Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor - Anatomy & Developmental Biology Clayton campus Level D ($181,629 - $200,092) 7 Oct 2026 Join Monash University as an Associate Professor / Senior Lecturer and make a leading contribution to research and education in developmental biology. Business Manager Melbourne City campus HEW 8 ($124,343 - $137,251) 22 Sep 2026 The Cranlana Centre for Ethical Leadership (CCEL) is seeking an exceptional Business Manager to partner closely with our Chief Executive Officer in translating strategic vision into operational success. Senior Strategic Analyst Clayton campus HEW 8 ($124,343 - $137,251) 22 Sep 2026 Join the Enterprise Intelligence 