    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697781/data-migration-analyst-smst": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional IT 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio eSolutions 1 Level / Salary HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 1 New Search Data Migration Analyst - SMST Job No.: 697781 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Fixed-term appointment until 30 June 2027 Remuneration: A competitive remuneration package will apply Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The Data Migration Analyst will join the Student Management System Transformation (SMST) Program, supporting the Data Migration Lead in delivering an end to end data migration solution to enable migration of data from existing Monash systems, to (primarily) a new Student Management System (SMS). We are looking for a detail-oriented and highly skilled analyst, who will ensure the accuracy, integrity and security of data during this complex data migration. This role will involve collaboration with cross-functional teams, including business analysts, developers, testers, external vendors and business stakeholders, ensuring seamless and efficient data loads and post migration validation processes. The ideal candidate has strong analytical skills, a keen eye for detail, and the required technical skills to develop data extraction processes, solve data management issues, provide high-quality data conversion and deliver reporting and dashboarding for data validation/reconciliation purposes. The ideal candidate will have; Demonstrated experience with data migration in a large and complex environment with varying levels of data quality. Strong proficiency with migration tools, data mapping, profiling, cleansing and quality assurance. Expertise in developing complex end to end ETL processes, interactive data visualisations, dashboards and reports using Databricks and Power BI. Strong proficiency in SQL and performance optimization. Superior communication skills to liaise with business and technical stakeholders Strong numeracy, analytical, and problem-solving abilities with the capability to identify challenges and recommend actionable solutions Excellent time management and attention to detail to meet deadlines and maintain accuracy Ability to work effectively as part of a team and exercise independence, judgment, and initiative Familiarity with Python and Callista data is desirable About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Send us a copy of your latest CV along with a cover letter (max 2 pages) that addresses your suitability for the role. A document addressing the Key Selection Criteria is not required. Please refer to  \" How to apply for Monash Jobs \" Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Ms Patricia Soto, Project Manager, Patricia.Soto@Monash.edu Position Description: Data Migration Analyst - SMST Applications Close: Monday 12 October 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Data Migration Analyst - SMST Clayton campus HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 12 Oct 2026 We are looking for a detail-oriented and highly skilled analyst, who will ensure the accuracy, integrity and security of data during this complex data migration from the existing Student Management system, Kallista to a new Student Management System (SMS) with Elucien. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Data Migration Analyst - SMST Clayton campus HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 12 Oct 202