    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/688565/manager-linux-platforms": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional IT 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Continuing (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio eSolutions 1 Level / Salary HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 1 New Search Manager – Linux Platforms Job No.: 688565 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing Full Time Remuneration: $145,062 - $153,976 HEW 09 (plus 17% superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Lead the future of Monash University’s enterprise Linux platforms and supporting automation services in a role combining technical leadership, people leadership and strategic impact. As the Manager – Linux Platforms , you will lead the Linux Platforms and Delivery teams, ensuring critical Linux services supporting enterprise, teaching and research systems are secure, resilient, highly available and fit for the future across complex hybrid cloud environments. You will drive the modernisation of Monash’s Linux capability through automation, Infrastructure as Code, observability, platform engineering and AI-enabled operations , while shaping platform roadmaps, lifecycle strategies and continuous improvement initiatives. In this role you will provide trusted technical leadership, manage risk and investment, and build high-performing teams. While strong technical credibility is essential, this is a leadership role not a primary hands-on engineering position providing the opportunity to set direction, empower technical specialists and shape the future of Linux services at scale within Monash. Key Selection Criteria Proven leadership of high-performing technical teams, with a strong focus on capability development, accountability and service excellence. Extensive enterprise Linux platform experience , with strong expertise across Red Hat Enterprise Linux and/or Ubuntu, including platform lifecycle, performance, availability, security, patching, capacity and operational management at scale. Strong automation and configuration management expertise , particularly Ansible, Puppet or equivalent, with demonstrated success standardising Linux builds, configuration, compliance and operational processes Strong expertise in Infrastructure as Code, DevOps and platform engineering , delivering scalable, standardised and repeatable infrastructure services. Experience embedding observability, i ntelligent monitoring, automation and AI-enabled/AIOps capabilities to improve reliability and operational efficiency. Demonstrated experience managing budgets, forecasting, vendor relationships, licensing and cost optimisation within complex ICT environments. Strong strategic, risk and service management capability , including lifecycle planning, operational support, incident management, disaster recovery and compliance. Exceptional stakeholder engagement, communication and influencing skills, with the credibility to provide expert technical advice and lead enterprise-wide initiatives To Apply Simply send us a copy of your latest CV along with a cover letter that outlines your suitability for this role. A statement addressing Key Selection Criteria is not required. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Learn more about Monash . Be part of our story. Work with us to #ChangeIt . Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . Enquiries: Justin Robins, Group Manager Server Cloud and Compute Platforms, Justin.Robins@monash.edu Position Description: Manager - Linux Platforms Applications Close: Friday 25th September 2026, 11:59 PM AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Manager – Linux Platforms Clayton campus HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 25 Sep 2026 Lead Monash’s enterprise Linux platforms and automation services, combining technical and people leadership with strategic impact. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Manager – Linux Platforms Clayton campus HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 25 Sep 2026 Lead Monash’s