    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/688774/rapid-application-engineer": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional IT 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Continuing (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio eSolutions 1 Level / Salary HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 1 New Search Rapid Application Engineer Job No.: 688774 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: $110,527 - $121,227 HEW 07 plus 17% employer superannuation Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join a dynamic team at the intersection of research, technology and commercial innovation, where you’ll turn emerging ideas and research prototypes into digital solutions with real-world impact. As a Rapid Application Engineer , you’ll work across the full product development lifecycle, from exploring problems and shaping concepts through to prototyping, engineering and production. Working closely with researchers, designers, industry partners and technical specialists, you’ll have the opportunity to translate complex technologies, including AI and machine learning, into intuitive, scalable and commercially viable applications. You’ll combine strong software engineering capability with a user-centred mindset, leveraging modern technologies such as React, TypeScript, Node.js and cloud platforms including GCP/Firebase and AWS. This is an opportunity to play a pivotal role in bridging the gap between research innovation and industry application, with the autonomy to solve complex problems, experiment with new technologies and deliver high-quality digital experiences that move ideas from proof-of-concept to meaningful commercial outcomes. Key Selection Criteria Demonstrated experience developing production-ready applications using JavaScript/TypeScript, React and Node.js , with modern cloud and serverless architectures across GCP/Firebase or AWS . Strong knowledge of modern software engineering practices, including coding standards, testing, version control, CI/CD, cloud deployment and application infrastructure. Solid understanding of system design and application architecture, including RESTful/GraphQL APIs, data flows, UI state management, authentication and data integration. Demonstrated ability to translate complex concepts, research prototypes or emerging technologies into practical digital solutions, with a strong focus on usability and user experience. Highly developed communication, collaboration and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively with researchers, designers, industry partners and technical teams. Strong organisation, judgement and initiative, with the ability to work autonomously, manage competing priorities and deliver outcomes in a fast-moving and ambiguous environment. A demonstrated curiosity and willingness to learn, with the adaptability to embrace emerging technologies, tools and methodologies and contribute to continuous innovation. Apply now and bring your expertise to the heart of research and technology innovation! About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We make tangible contributions because our purpose is clear; to deliver positive economic, social and environmental impact in resolving the global challenges of our age. At the core of achieving this purpose is the diversity of our staff. We welcome and value everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. When you come to work, you can be yourself, be a change-maker and develop your career in exciting ways. This is why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must include your latest CV and Cover Letter outlining your suitability to the role. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Steven Gardner, Group Manager Research and Grad Research, steven.gardner@monash.edu Position Description: Rapid Application Engineer Applications Close: Sunday 27th September 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their 