    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697406/lecturer-senior-lecturer-radiographer": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Academic - Teaching and Research 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Continuing (Part-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary Level C ($150,841 - $173,931) 1 New Search Lecturer / Senior Lecturer - Radiographer Job No.: 697406 Location: Clayton and Peninsula campus Employment Type: Part-time, fraction (0.8) Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: Pro-rata of $123,138 - $146,228 pa Level B / $150,841 - $173,931 pa Level C (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity As a Lecturer (Level B) or Senior Lecturer (Level C) in Radiography, you will help shape the next generation of medical imaging professionals through high-quality teaching, clinical engagement and scholarly and research activity. Joining Monash University’s Department of Medical Imaging and Radiation Sciences, you will contribute to the Bachelor of Radiography and Medical Imaging (Honours), while supporting undergraduate and postgraduate teaching and developing your scholarly, research and professional profile. At Level C, you will make a significant contribution to teaching and research, with opportunities to coordinate subjects, lead research projects and supervise honours and postgraduate research students. This position will contribute to innovative face-to-face, online and blended teaching across radiography and medical imaging, drawing on contemporary research and industry practice. You will contribute to lectures, tutorials, practical and clinical learning, assessment and subject coordination, while supporting students across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. You will also undertake scholarly and research activities, contribute to publications and research projects, and develop professional and clinical partnerships. At Level B, you will make a strong contribution to teaching, scholarly activity and professional engagement, with opportunities to develop research capability and contribute to subject and curriculum development. At Level C, you will take a greater role in research activity, subject or course coordination, postgraduate supervision and the development of professional and clinical partnerships. To be successful in this role you will have a Bachelor’s or Master degree in Medical Imaging/Radiography or equivalent accreditation and standing, and ideally a doctoral or master’s by research qualification in Medical Imaging/Radiography or a related field. You will have current or eligible registration with the Medical Radiation Practice Board of Australia (MRPBA) and a radiation licence. You will bring tertiary teaching experience in radiography and medical imaging, with expertise in areas such as CT, MRI and/or image interpretation, alongside demonstrated engagement in scholarly and research activities. For Level B, you will demonstrate the capacity to contribute effectively to teaching, subject material development, research and professional activities. For Level C, you will demonstrate a strong record of tertiary teaching and research, including subject coordination, research publications, postgraduate supervision and the capacity to develop research projects and professional partnerships. The Department - Medical Imaging and Radiation Sciences The Department’s staff are deeply engaged in clinical, educational, and laboratory-based research, partnering with leading institutions across Australia and internationally. These dynamic research activities open doors for graduates and qualified medical radiation practitioners to pursue higher degrees such as a Master of Philosophy or PhD. Committed to lifelong learning, the Department supports the professional growth of radiographers, radiation therapists, and nuclear medicine technologists through advanced practice pathways in the Master of Advanced Health Care Practice. Learn more about Medical Imaging and Radiation Sciences Connect with Monash Department of Medical Imaging and Radiation Sciences (DMIRS) on LinkedIn The School - School of Primary and Allied Health Care (SPAHC) SPAHC harnesses a range of expertise, including physiotherapy, occupational therapy, paramedicine, podiatry, social work and medical imaging and radiation sciences. Our cross-disciplinary approach addresses society's most vital questions. Learn more about Primary and Allied Health Care About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Monash University invites applications from candidates who can demonstrate valid and current Australian work rights. For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Sergio Uribe Arancibia, School of Primary and Allied Health Care, Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences  +61 3 (9905 3119) Position Description: Level B - Lecturer - Radiographer Level C - Senior Lecturer - Radiographer Applications Close: Friday 9 October 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Please submit your application as soon as possible for this fabulous opportunity to join Monash University. Interviews will be held as strong applicants are identified. Applications will close when the role has been filled. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Lecturer / Senior Lecturer - Radiographer Clayton campus Level C ($150,841 - $173,931) 9 Oct 2026 Monash University's School of Primary and Allied Health Care are seeking a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer within Radiography, for a short term appointment that will contribute to the delivery of the Bachelor of Radiography and Medical Imaging (Honours) and support undergraduate and postgraduate teaching within the Department. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Lecturer / Senior Lecturer - Radiographer Clayton campus Level C ($150,841 - $173,931) 9 Oct 2026 Monash University's School of Primary and Allied Health Care are seeking a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer within Radiography, for a short term appointment that will contribute to the delivery of the Bachelor of Radiography and Medical Imaging (Honours) and support undergraduate and postgraduate teaching within the Department. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 0