    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697562/research-fellow-data-scientist-wearable-technologies-digital-health-artificial-intelligence": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Academic - Research Only 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary Level B ($123,138 - $146,228) 1 New Search Research Fellow, Data Scientist (Wearable Technologies, Digital Health & Artificial Intelligence) Job No.: 697562 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 3-years fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $123,138 - $146,228 pa Level B (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact in digital health, wearables and AI-driven research Join our Research Fellow team and help shape the future of digital health Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas driving innovation in data science and health The Opportunity We have an opportunity available for a Research Fellow, Data Scientist to join the Professor Stamatakis research program and contribute to the advancement of digital health and data science capability within an internationally connected research program, with a focus on wearables, data processing pipelines, machine learning and generative AI applied to physical activity and sleep research. The position will contribute to the development of an AI-based behaviour change tool and support data-sharing IT infrastructure, while contributing to research, publications, grant applications and collaborations with leading academic and external partners. The position will develop and validate wearable data algorithms, software tools and pipelines supporting large-scale, multi-cohort research. It will contribute to the ProPASS federated data analysis platform, including testing, documentation, quality assurance and partner onboarding. The role will apply machine learning and generative AI, including LLM-based conversational AI, and translate technical capabilities through workshops, stakeholder engagement and research outputs. We are seeking someone with a doctoral qualification in data science, computer science, biomedical engineering, statistics or a related quantitative discipline, or equivalent qualifications or research experience. You will bring demonstrated skills in statistical analysis, research publication and proposal preparation, together with knowledge and experience in machine learning, generative AI or LLM-based systems, cloud computing, and the design and validation of algorithms for high-volume quantitative or sensor-derived data. Experience with wearable data, health or population health research, federated data environments, data security and governance will be also be highly regarded, alongside strong communication, organisational and collaborative skills. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to a multidisciplinary research program at the intersection of digital health, wearables, data science and AI—apply now to be part of this collaborative and internationally connected research environment. Monash University seeks applicants for this opportunity who are able to demonstrate present valid and current Australian work rights. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Associate Professor Matthew Ahmadi, Matthew.Ahmadi@monash.edu Position Description: Research Fellow, Data Scientist Applications Close: Thursday 1 October 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Clos