    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697564/research-fellow-cognitive-ageing-dementia": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Academic - Research Only 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 1 New Search Research Fellow, Cognitive Ageing & Dementia Job No.: 697564 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12-months fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $86,195 - $116,981 pa Level A (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact as a Research Fellow at Monash Join our inclusive, collaborative research community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people behind them The Opportunity The Healthy Brain Hub is seeking a Research Fellow to contribute to improving access to cognitive assessment through digital brain health approaches. Based within the School of Psychological Sciences and Turner Institute for Brain and Mental Health, the position will support study coordination, data collection and management, data analysis and evaluation of a digital brain health assessment platform across clinical settings. The role will also contribute to research protocols, ethics applications, funding activities and research outputs. The position will contribute to the scientific program through the analysis and interpretation of research data, preparation of manuscripts and conference presentations, and the development of research questions and ideas. It will also support the research environment through collaboration with colleagues and the supervision and mentoring of research assistants and students. The role provides an opportunity to apply advanced statistical methods, including mixed effects, survival, growth curve and prediction models, to research in neuropsychology, epidemiology, neurodegenerative disease and cognitive disorders. We are seeking someone with a doctoral qualification, or near completion of a doctoral qualification, in Psychology, Neuroepidemiology, Neuroscience, Neurology or a related discipline, together with demonstrated analytical and manuscript preparation skills and a record of refereed research publications. Knowledge of neuropsychology and epidemiological methods, advanced statistical analysis using programs such as R or SAS, and strong planning, organisational, communication and problem-solving skills are also important for this role. Join the Healthy Brain Hub and contribute to research that is helping advance accessible approaches to cognitive assessment and brain health. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Please ensure your cover letter clearly outlines how your skills and experience align with the requirements of this role particularly in the area of neuropsychology and knowledge of epidemiological methods, particularly in neurodegenerative or cognitive disorders. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Yen Ying Lim, Yenying.Lim@monash.edu Position Description: Research Fellow - Cognitive Ageing & Dementia Applications Close: Thursday 8 October 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Fellow, Cognitive Ageing & Dementia Clayton campus Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 8 Oct 2026 Join as Research Fellow and support innovative research improving access to digital cognitive assessments. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Fellow, Cognitive Ageing & Dementia Clayton campus Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 8 Oct 2026 Join as Research Fellow and support innovative research improving access to digital cognitive assessments. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
