    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697708/research-fellow": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Academic - Research Only 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Science 1 Level / Salary Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 1 New Search Research Fellow Job No.: 697708 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 3 year fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $86,195 - $116,981 pa (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Monash University's School of Physics and Astronomy in the Faculty of Science sits at the forefront of discovery, attracting researchers who want their work to matter beyond the laboratory. This fixed-term, full-time Research Fellow position offers the scope to drive original inquiry within a collaborative and well-resourced academic environment at the Clayton campus. Working within an active research group, this position will be in support of a project to develop and demonstrate micro-scale intracranial probes to sense the extremely small magnetic fields resulting from the currents flowing along nerve cells due to brain activity. The probes to be developed will utilise a quantum sensor based on optically detectable defects in diamond that are sensitive to magnetic fields. To be appointable into this role you will hold a PhD in Physics, Astronomy, or a closely related discipline (conferred or near completion), possess strong analytical and problem-solving skills applied to experimental or theoretical research and experience with relevant instrumentation, computational methods, or modelling tools specific to your subfield. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Kristian Helmerson, Professor and Research Director, School of Physics and Astronomy - kristian.helmerson@monash.edu.au Position Description: Research Fellow Applications Close: October 7, 2026 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Fellow Clayton campus Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 7 Oct 2026 Working within an active research group, this position will be in support of a project to develop and demonstrate micro-scale intracranial probes to sense the extremely small magnetic fields resulting from the currents flowing along nerve cells due to brain activity. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Fellow Clayton campus Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 7 Oct 2026 Working within an active research group, this position will be in support of a project to develop and demonstrate micro-scale intracranial probes to sense the extremely small magnetic fields resulting from the currents flowing along nerve cells due to brain activity. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates