    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697945/senior-lecturer-associate-professor-anatomy-developmental-biology": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Academic - Teaching and Research 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Continuing (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary Level D ($181,629 - $200,092) 1 New Search Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor - Anatomy & Developmental Biology Job No.: 697945 Location: Clayton Campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: $150,841 - $173,931 pa Level C / $181,629 - $200,092 pa Level D (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join Monash University as an Associate Professor / Senior Lecturer and make a leading contribution to research and education in developmental biology. You will bring expertise in developmental biology, reproductive health or stem cell biology, advancing research excellence while delivering outstanding teaching across developmental biology, histology, Biomedical Science, postgraduate programs and medical education. At Level D, you will provide recognised disciplinary leadership and distinction; at Level C, you will make a major contribution to research, scholarship and teaching. This position will be responsible for delivering engaging lectures, tutorials, practical classes, seminars and workshops; developing and coordinating high-quality curriculum, learning materials and assessment; and supporting effective teaching teams and student learning. You will supervise honours, postgraduate and PhD students, and contribute to postgraduate training. You will also lead and undertake original impactful research that generates high-quality publications, attracts competitive external funding and aligns with the department’s culture and priorities. You will play a significant role in research engagement and team leadership, while contributing to the broader academic community. At Level D, you will additionally provide substantial leadership through mentoring, course coordination, and discipline-building activities nationally and internationally; at Level C, you will demonstrate strong research leadership and contribute actively to departmental and faculty planning. To be successful in this role you will have a doctoral qualification and significant experience in developmental and cell biology and/or reproductive health, with a strong record of high-quality research publications, external research funding and postgraduate supervision. You will bring demonstrated excellence in teaching developmental biology and histology, including curriculum and assessment development and course coordination, alongside strong interpersonal, collaborative and mentoring skills. Level D candidates will additionally demonstrate distinction in their discipline, significant leadership, a sustained record of research funding and scholarly achievement, and the capacity to mentor colleagues and lead the discipline. Level C candidates will demonstrate emerging or established research leadership and a strong capacity to lead research projects and teams. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Helen Abud, helen.abud@monash.edu Position Description: Level C - Senior Lecturer Level D - Associate Professor Applications Close: Wednesday 7 October 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send yo