, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional Business Development and Industry Engagement 1 Locations Campus Melbourne City campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Vice-Chancellor and President 1 Level / Salary HEW 8 ($124,343 - $137,251) 1 New Search Business Manager Job No.: 696957 Location: Melbourne City campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Fixed-term appointment from 3 November 2026 - 21 November 2027 Remuneration: $124,343 - $137,251 pa HEW Level 08 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The Cranlana Centre for Ethical Leadership (CCEL) is seeking an exceptional Business Manager to partner closely with our Chief Executive Officer in translating strategic vision into operational success. In this high-impact leadership role, you will oversee end-to-end business operations, drive financial health, modernise systems and empower a high-performing team to scale our mission. As Business Manager, you will serve as a strategic driver and operational anchor for CCEL, balancing high-level strategic thinking with hands-on delivery. Working closely with senior leadership, you will lead operational strategy, organisational planning and standard operating procedures to optimise efficiency, scalability and measurable performance against strategic KPIs. You will take full charge of financial oversight and commercial management - directing annual budgets, forecasting, financial analysis and client agreements to ensure long-term viability and growth. A critical element of this role involves maintaining rigorous organisational governance and risk management, while ensuring seamless alignment with University policies and regulatory frameworks. You will oversee organisational infrastructure, directing CRM systems, IT platforms, procurement and emerging technologies to streamline service delivery across major events, open enrolment programmes and strategic projects. To thrive in this environment, you are a seasoned operations executive with a proven track record in financial oversight, digital infrastructure management and process improvement within a university, non-profit or complex organisational setting. You bring strong leadership and people management skills, capable of nurturing a collaborative, high-performing team while managing critical relationships across internal University networks, external partners and senior executive stakeholders. The ideal candidate should hold postgraduate qualifications alongside extensive relevant management experience, or possess an equivalent combination of high-level industry experience, education, and training. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Rachel Byrne, Senior Operations Manager, +61 3 9903 8889 Position Description: Business Manager Applications Close: Tuesday 22 September 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Business Manager Melbourne City campus HEW 8 ($124,343 - $137,251) 22 Sep 2026 The Cranlana Centre for Ethical Leadership (CCEL) is seeking an exceptional Business Manager to partner closely with our Chief Executive Officer in translating 