, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional IT 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Continuing (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio eSolutions 1 Level / Salary HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 1 New Search Manager Cyber Security Operations Centre Job No.: 692608 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: $145,062 - $153,976 pa HEW Level 09 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Join Monash University cyber team in a key operational leadership role responsible for the performance, coordination, and continuous improvement of a 24x7 Cyber Security Operations Centre (CSOC) supporting a large, complex and globally connected environment. As the Manager – CSOC , you will be responsible for driving the operational excellence, consistency, and maturity of the cyber security operations centre (CSOC) ensuring that detection, response, cyber investigations, and CSIRT functions operate in a cohesive, efficient, and risk-aligned manner. You will standardise and optimise the CSOC operating model , uplift service delivery, and ensure the function is positioned to respond effectively to an evolving threat landscape spanning cloud, identity, SaaS, supply chain, and AI-enabled risks. You will act as the senior escalation point during major cyber incidents , providing coordination, communication, and executive-level decision support. At the same time, you will own the end-to-end performance of the CSOC, including KPI definition, service metrics, reporting, and continuous improvement initiatives that drive measurable outcomes. A key aspect of the role is stakeholder engagement and influence. You will regularly present operational insights, risk posture, and performance outcomes to senior stakeholders, translating complex cyber concepts into clear, actionable intelligence that supports decision-making. Working across technology, risk, governance, and external partners, you will ensure the cyber security operations centre is aligned with organisational risk appetite, regulatory obligations, and strategic priorities, while building a sustainable and high-performing operational capability. About You You are a proven cyber security operations leader with the ability to balance operational discipline, stakeholder engagement, and strategic uplift . You are comfortable operating in complex environments, leading distributed teams, and driving clarity and performance in high-pressure situations. You will bring: Proven experience leading or managing a Security Operations Centre (SOC/CSOC) within a complex enterprise environment, including geographically distributed teams Strong expertise across detection, response, investigation, and CSIRT functions , with the ability to standardise and mature existing SOC capabilities Demonstrated ownership of operational performance , including defining KPIs, managing service metrics, and delivering clear, data-driven reporting Experience providing leadership during major cyber incidents , including coordination, escalation, and executive decision support Strong stakeholder management and communication skills , including the ability to present to senior audiences and influence outcomes Experience translating technical cyber security issues into clear risk-based insights and recommendations Solid understanding of security frameworks and standards such as ISO 27001/27002, NIST, CIS , and familiarity with MITRE ATT&CK and modern threat landscapes Experience working with third-party providers or managed services , ensuring accountability and service quality About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We make tangible contributions because our purpose is clear; to deliver positive economic, social and environmental impact in resolving the global challenges of our age. At the core of achieving this purpose is the diversity of our staff. We welcome and value everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. When you come to work, you can be yourself, be a change-maker and develop your career in exciting ways. This is why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Raj Udayanga , Cyber Security Operations Group Manager, lmsnmbuqwx@p.monash.edu Position Description: Manager - Cyber Security Operations Centre Applications Close: Tuesday 22nd September 2026 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Manager Cyber Security Operations Centre Clayton campus HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 22 Sep 2026 Lead Monash’s 24x7 CSOC, driving performance, standardisation, and continuous improvement across global cyber security operations! Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Manager Cyber Security Operations Centre Clayton campus HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 22 Sep 2026 Lead Monash’s 24x7 CSOC, driving performance, standardisation, and continuous improvement across global cyber security operations! Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens