    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698225/phd-scholarship-opportunity-developing-the-next-generation-of-evidencebased-rheumatology-researchers": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Scholarship 1 Locations Off-campus St Kilda Road 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary New Search PhD Scholarship Opportunity - Developing the Next Generation of Evidence-Based Rheumatology Researchers Job No: 698225 Location: Monash University School of Public Health and Preventative Medicine (509 St Kilda Rd, Melbourne) Employment Type: Full time Duration: 3 years Supervisors: The successful applicant will be supervised by internationally recognised leaders in evidence-based medicine, guideline methodology and rheumatology, including Professor Rachelle Buchbinder and Dr Samuel Whittle, supported by an experienced multidisciplinary research team. Remuneration: The successful applicant will receive a Research Living Allowance, at current value of $41,100 AUD per annum at the 2027 full-time rate, indexed plus allowances as per RTP stipend scholarship conditions at www.monash.edu/graduate-research/study/scholarships/fees-scholarships/scholarship-policy-and-procedures. Join a world-leading research team developing the future of evidence-based rheumatology. Applications are invited for a fully supported PhD scholarship at Monash University to undertake innovative research in the development, implementation and evaluation of living clinical practice guidelines in rheumatology. Based within the Australia and New Zealand Musculoskeletal (ANZMUSC) Clinical Trials Network, this project offers the opportunity to contribute to internationally recognised research that directly informs clinical care for people with rheumatic diseases. About the Project Living guidelines represent a transformative approach to evidence synthesis and clinical guideline development. By combining continuous evidence surveillance with state-of-the-art systematic review methods, GRADE methodology and digital guideline platforms, living guidelines ensure that clinical recommendations remain current as new evidence emerges. ANZMUSC has been a global leader in this field, developing the world’s first living guidelines for inflammatory arthritis. The successful candidate will contribute to the ongoing development and evaluation of these internationally recognised guidelines while undertaking original research suitable for a PhD. Research Focus The successful candidate will undertake research that could include: ·         Development and evaluation of living evidence synthesis methods ·         Systematic reviews and meta-analyses ·         Translation of research evidence into clinical practice recommendations ·         Application of GRADE methodology and Evidence-to-Decision frameworks ·         Use and evaluation of digital guideline platforms (MAGICapp) ·         Implementation science and knowledge translation in rheumatology ·         Investigation of innovative approaches to maintaining high-quality, evidence-based clinical guidelines ·         Evaluating the impact of guideline recommendations on clinical practice in patient care The exact research questions will be developed in consultation with the supervisory team and tailored to the successful candidate’s interests. Training Opportunities This PhD provides comprehensive training in: ·         Systematic review and meta-analysis ·         Evidence synthesis and critical appraisal ·         GRADE guideline development methodology ·         Living evidence methods ·         Clinical epidemiology ·         Scientific writing and publication ·         Research presentation and stakeholder engagement ·         Collaboration with multidisciplinary and consumer-inclusive research teams The candidate will work alongside an experienced evidence synthesis team, guideline developers, clinicians, statisticians, librarians and consumer representatives. Supervision The successful applicant will be supervised by internationally recognised leaders in evidence-based medicine, guideline methodology  and rheumatology, including Professor Rachelle Buchbinder and Dr Samuel Whittle, supported by an experienced multidisciplinary research team. Research Environment As part of ANZMUSC, the successful candidate will join Australia’s leading collaborative musculoskeletal clinical research network, working alongside more than 400 researchers, clinicians, consumers and policymakers across Australia and New Zealand. The successful candidate will become part of an internationally respected research program at the forefront of living evidence and guideline methodology. During the PhD, the successful candidate will have opportunities to: ·         Publish in high-impact peer-reviewed journals ·         Participate in National and international collaborations ·         Deliver conference presentations ·         Participate in world-leading methodological research ·         Develop skills applicable to careers in academia, clinical research and evidence-based healthcare Flexible working arrangements are available, with many aspects of the research able to be undertaken remotely, making this an excellent opportunity for candidates based in metropolitan, regional or rural locations. Eligibility Applicants should have: ·         Eligibility to enrol in a PhD at Monash University ·         A medical degree or honours degree (or equivalent) in a relevant health or biomedical discipline ·         An interest in evidence-based medicine, rheumatology, epidemiology or clinical research ·         Strong analytical and communication skills ·         A commitment to improving healthcare through high-quality research Previous experience in systematic reviews or guideline development is desirable but not essential. How to Apply Interested applicants should contact Grace O’Donohue ( grace.odonohue@monash.edu ) for further information regarding the project, scholarship details and application process. Application Close Date: Sunday 04/10/2026 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes PhD Scholarship Opportunity: Developing the Next Generation of Evidence-Based Rheumatology Researchers St Kilda Road 4 Oct 2026 Applications are invited for a fully supported PhD scholarship at Monash University to undertake innovative research in the development, implementation and evaluation of living clinical practice guidelines in rheumatology. Based within the Australia and New Zealand Musculoskeletal (ANZMUSC) Clinical Trials Network, this project offers the opportunity to contribute to internationally recognised research that directly informs clinical care for people with rheumatic diseases.. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes PhD Scholarship Opportunity: Developing the Next Generation of Evidence-Based Rheumatology Researchers St Kilda Road 4 Oct 2026 Applications are invited for a fully supported PhD scholarship at Monash University to undertake innovative research in the development, implementation and evaluation of living clinical practice guidelines in rheumatology. Based within the Australia and New Zealand Musculoskeletal (ANZMUSC) Clinical Trials Network, this project offers the opportunity to contribute to internationally recognised research that directly informs clinical care for people with rheumatic diseases.. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
