    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697785/erp-senior-business-analyst": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional IT 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio eSolutions 1 Level / Salary HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 1 New Search ERP - Senior Business Analyst - HR stream Job No.: 697785 Location: Mulgrave Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Fixed-term appointment until August 2027 Remuneration: $145,062 to $153,976 pa HEW Level 09 (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity We are seeking a forward-thinking Senior Business Analyst ready to spearhead a transformation in a high-impact University environment. As an expert Analyst in the ERP Project Team, you will operate with a high degree of autonomy, and lead the critical analysis, design, and continuous improvement of core HR, payroll operations, recruitment, and workforce insights. Using design thinking methodologies, you will translate complex organisational challenges into modern, automated, and intelligent service models that enhance the overall employee experience. What You’ll Bring to the Role A collaborative team player who builds strong relationships across diverse stakeholder groups and brings positive energy to the delivery of complex transformation. Demonstrated design thinking & vision for a future-state applying design thinking to map user journeys, articulate HR business problems, and explore AI-enabled ERP capabilities, automation, and decision support. Proven HR & ERP expertise based on an extensive background leading current and future-state analysis across People & Culture, Payroll, and cross-functional operations within large-scale ERP transformation programs. Superior consulting, negotiation, and relationship skills to bridge functional HR needs with a group-wide scope (Finance, Research, Technology enablement). Exceptional capacity to synthesise complex, multi-source data into strategic insights, business cases, and workable solutions. Highly skilled in facilitating high-engagement workshops, framing trade-offs, and building organisational change readiness across affected business units. Key Requirements to be successful in this role include Thorough, end-to-end understanding of modern HR operating models, payroll systems, talent acquisition, and workforce analytics—specifically within large-scale multi-jurisdiction/global ERP environments. Forward-looking mindset regarding how AI, intelligent automation, and predictive analytics can streamline service delivery, enhance employee and manager self-service, and support executive decision-making. Strong quantitative and conceptual analytical skills with a proven ability to process disjointed, multi-source data to build sound business cases and trace metrics back to strategic outcomes. Pragmatic, and proactive approach to problem solving and building change readiness with empathy through collaborative, co-designed workshops and risk communication. This is a high-visibility opportunity to influence executive decision-making, direct cutting-edge process design, and leave a lasting mark on the University’s operational landscape. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Ms Siew Ying Cheong, Principal Business Analyst. Contact: SiewYing.Cheong@Monash.edu . Position Description: Senior Business Analyst - ERP Applications Close: Wednesday 30 September 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes ERP - Senior Business Analyst Clayton campus HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 30 Sep 2026 We are seeking a forward-thinking Senior Business Analyst ready to spearhead a transformation in a high-impact University environment. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes ERP - Senior Business Analyst Clayton campus HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 30 Sep 2026 We are seeking a forward-thinking Senior Business Analyst ready to spearhead a transformation in a high-impact University environment. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright