    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698400/casual-learning-designer": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional Teaching Support 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Casual 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 1 New Search Learning Designer Job No.: 698400 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Casual part time, 4 hours per week, from 13 Oct 2026 to 14 Dec 2026 Remuneration: Casual HEW 7 rates will apply Be inspired, every day Take your career in exciting, rewarding directions Be a part of an inclusive, collaborative community The Opportunity The School of Psychological Sciences is seeking a casual Learning Designer to support the redevelopment and alignment of two foundational psychology units across the Graduate Diploma of Psychology (GDP) and Bachelor of Psychology (BPsych) programs. Working collaboratively with academic staff, you will help shape engaging, accessible and inclusive learning experiences, with a focus on Universal Design for Learning (UDL), active and relational learning, and effective synchronous and asynchronous learning design. This is a short-term project involving 40 hours of work (approximately 4 hours per week), where you will bring your learning design expertise to an iterative and collaborative co-design process. You will review existing learning materials, provide advice on contemporary learning design and pedagogy, and identify opportunities to improve accessibility, engagement, navigation, consistency and alignment with learning outcomes across both programs. About You You will be an experienced Learning Designer with demonstrated expertise in designing engaging, inclusive and accessible learning experiences across different modes of delivery. You will have strong knowledge of Universal Design for Learning (UDL), and experience designing for both asynchronous and synchronous learning environments, with an understanding of how to create active, relational and engaging learning experiences across different modes of delivery that support diverse student cohorts . You will be collaborative, proactive and comfortable working in an evolving project environment where requirements may not always be fully defined. You will bring sound judgement, creative thinking and the confidence to provide evidence-informed learning design advice and  recommendations to academic staff, while working collaboratively to develop learning activities that effectively scaffold student learning, support engagement with assessment, and enable the achievement of learning outcomes. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Learn more about Monash . Join the pursuit of our purpose to build a better future for ourselves and our communities - #ChangeIt with us. To Apply To apply, please submit your application via the “Apply Now” button. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. Should you require any specific support or adjustments throughout the recruitment process and beyond, please get in touch at hr-recruitment@monash.edu and we'll be happy to assist. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Dr Lilani Arulkadacham, Senior Lecturer, School of Psychological Sciences & Acting Director of Education (Foundational Psychology), lilani.arulkadacham@monash.edu Applications Close: Wednesday 30th of September, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Casual - Learning Designer Clayton campus HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 30 Sep 2026 A casual opportunity to develop two Graduate Diploma of Psychology units for engaging, accessible and inclusive asynchronous online learning experiences. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Casual - Learning Designer Clayton campus HEW 7 ($110,527 - $121,227) 30 Sep 2026 A casual opportunity to develop two Graduate Diploma of Psychology units for engaging, accessible and inclusive asynchronous online learning experiences. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
