    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697625/erp-senior-finance-specialist-controlled-entities": {
      "title": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional Finance 1 Locations Off-campus Mulgrave 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Chief Financial Officer and Senior Vice-President 1 Level / Salary HEW10A ($191,131) 1 New Search ERP Senior Finance Specialist - Controlled Entities Job No.: 697625 Location: Mulgrave Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12-month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $191,131 pa HEW Level 10A + (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Reporting to the ERP Finance Lead, the focus of the ERP Senior Finance Specialist – Controlled Entities role will be to apply deep, specialised domain expertise to guide the design, configuration, and build of the new Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system. Serving as a critical bridge between business operations and the technical implementation team, you will hold enterprise-wide accountability for designing, establishing, and governing the financial architecture, management reporting structures, statutory compliance, and consolidation frameworks across all Monash University controlled entities and international subsidiaries. What You'll Be Doing Leading ERP configuration and testing activities specific to controlled entity financial operations, including intercompany transactions and consolidation processes Partnering with finance and technology stakeholders to map current-state processes and translate requirements into system solutions Providing subject matter expertise on chart of accounts, financial reporting frameworks, and entity-level compliance obligations Supporting end-user training, documentation, and change management activities across impacted finance teams What You'll Bring Demonstrated experience in a senior finance or systems role within a large, complex organisation -  ideally with exposure to university controlled entities or government-related structures Hands-on ERP implementation or configuration experience, with strong knowledge of finance modules Solid understanding of Australian accounting standards and consolidation principles as they apply to controlled entities Proven ability to translate technical finance requirements into clear system and process documentation CPA or CA qualification, or equivalent professional experience Experience working within Monash University's financial systems environment, or familiarity with its entity structure, is highly regarded If you are a visionary finance professional ready to shape the future financial landscape of a global university, apply today. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Position Description: Senior Finance Specialist - Controlled Entities Applications Close: Thursday 1 October 2026 at 11:55PM AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes ERP - Senior Finance Specialist - Controlled Entities Mulgrave HEW10A ($191,131) 1 Oct 2026 Monash University is preparing to embark on a journey to upgrade our Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system. We're seeking an experience subject matter expert in Controlled Entities to join the team. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes ERP - Senior Finance Specialist - Controlled Entities Mulgrave H