, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional Finance 1 Locations Off-campus Mulgrave 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Chief Financial Officer and Senior Vice-President 1 Level / Salary HEW10C ($227,857) 1 New Search ERP Finance Lead Job No.: 697626 Location: Mulgrave Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12 month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $227,857 pa HEW Level 10C (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The ERP Finance Lead is a senior leadership role responsible for leading the finance transformation workstream within the University's Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) Program. The role is accountable for defining and delivering the future-state finance operating model, ensuring the ERP solution enables best-practice financial management, governance, reporting and compliance while supporting the University's long-term strategic objectives. What You'll Be Leading Lead end-to-end finance workstream activities across the ERP implementation lifecycle, from design workshops through to go-live and stabilisation Act as the primary liaison between finance stakeholders and the broader ERP project team, ensuring business requirements are accurately captured and delivered Review, validate and sign off on system configuration, data migration and finance process design outputs Identify risks and dependencies within the finance workstream and drive resolution in a structured, timely manner What You'll Bring Demonstrated experience leading finance workstreams within a large ERP implementation Strong technical understanding of core finance processes including general ledger, accounts payable, accounts receivable and financial reporting Proven ability to engage and influence finance stakeholders at all levels, from operational teams to senior leadership Experience working within a structured project methodology (waterfall, agile or hybrid) Tertiary qualifications in Finance, Accounting or a related discipline; CA/CPA advantageous Prior exposure to complex, multi-entity or public sector finance environments highly regarded This is a meaningful role for a finance professional who thrives in project environments, brings clarity to complexity, and understands that successful ERP delivery is as much about people and process as it is about technology. If you're ready to make a measurable contribution to a transformation of genuine scale, we'd welcome your application. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. 